I. IS THERE A DECADAL-SPECIFIC DEFECT LEFT, ONCE THE ARM IS JUDGED AGAINST ITSELF?
========================================================================
  arm          sd(dec)    own eps | null from ITS OWN trend+noise [5% .. 50% .. 95%]
  GCB 2025      0.0483      0.911 | 0.0261 .. 0.0472 .. 0.0734   INSIDE
  defaults      0.0393      0.638 | 0.0239 .. 0.0410 .. 0.0602   INSIDE
  ent26         0.0246      0.698 | 0.0165 .. 0.0303 .. 0.0489   INSIDE

  ⚠ THE NULL DRAWS WHITE NOISE while both arms' residuals are autocorrelated
    (rho +0.255/+0.193 vs the observations' +0.014), which INFLATES a decade sum's variance.
    So the arms' intervals here are if anything too NARROW, and they are INSIDE
    anyway -- the error runs in the direction that would have caught a defect.

